      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. Let me write an improved, more understandable version.\n\nThe test verifies that `URLCodec.encodeUrl` with a null BitSet (which causes it to fall back to the default `WWW_FORM_URL_SAFE` set) percent-encodes all 8 non-safe bytes: each unsafe byte becomes 3 bytes (`%XX`), so 8 × 3 = 24.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version preserves the exact same method calls and assertions while adding clear variable names (`inputBytes`, `encodedBytes`) and explanatory comments that describe why each byte gets percent-encoded and how the expected length of 24 is derived (8 non-safe bytes × 3 encoded bytes each)."
